# Cashier

Expo Router app. `app/` is routing. Feature UI lives in `src/`. Style with NativeWind. Send requests through `@horpynka/api-sdk`.

## Where code goes

- `app/` — layouts and screens. A screen composes feature components and loads its data. Keep the JSX thin.
- `src/routes/<feature>/components/<name>/` — UI for one screen. Home is `src/routes/home`. A receipt is `src/routes/receiptId`.
- `src/components/` — chrome shared by several routes, such as the header.
- `src/ui-kit/components/<name>/` — domain-free primitives: button, text field, modal. Add a story in `.rnstorybook/stories/` in the same change, following `Button.stories.tsx`.
- `src/contexts/<name>/` — React context, barreled from `index.ts`.
- `src/store/` — Zustand. One slice file per domain, composed in `src/store/index.ts`.
- `src/utils/<name>-service.ts` — a class and its singleton (`moneyService`, `dateFns`, `yupService`, `secureStoreService`).
- `src/initializers.ts` — the only place that calls `initApiClient`.

A component folder is `kebab-case` and holds `<name>.tsx` plus `index.ts`:

```ts
export { ActiveReceiptList } from './active-receipt-list';
```

## Routing

Tab screens live in `app/(app)/(tabs)/`. That layout already renders the rail, `Header`, and page padding. Auth gates stay in `app/_layout.tsx` via `Stack.Protected`. Read the session with `useSession()`.

Route files use a default export. Every other module uses a named export.

Leave `ios/`, `android/`, and `.expo/` alone.

`kitchen.tsx`, `menu.tsx`, `receipts/index.tsx`, and `+not-found.tsx` are Expo template leftovers. Follow `sign-in.tsx` and `app/(app)/(tabs)/index.tsx` instead.

## Components

ESLint is the style source: single quotes and semicolons. Older files that skip semicolons or use double quotes are drift. New code follows ESLint.

- Functions are `PascalCase`. Files and folders are `kebab-case`.
- Local props type is `Props`. Export a props type from ui-kit (`ButtonProps`) when callers need it.
- Cross-module imports use `@/src/...`. Imports inside one feature are relative.
- Import a primitive from its folder barrel: `@/src/ui-kit/components/button`.
- Import the hooks and types you use from `react`. Add a default `React` import only when you need the namespace (`React.ReactNode`).
- New press targets use `Pressable`.
- User-facing copy is Ukrainian.
- State that one screen owns stays in `useState`. Use Zustand when another screen reads it, as with the open receipt.

```tsx
type Props = {
  receipts: Order[];
};

export const ActiveReceiptList = ({ receipts }: Props) => {
  return (
    <FlatList
      data={receipts}
      contentContainerClassName="gap-3"
      renderItem={({ item }) => <ActiveReceiptCard data={item} />}
    />
  );
};
```

Skip empty `type Props = {}` and unused `props` parameters.

## Styling

Style with NativeWind `className`. New UI does not add `StyleSheet`.

Use the semantic tokens in `tailwind.config.js`: `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`, `text-card-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-primary`, `bg-destructive`, `bg-muted`. A color that already has a token stays a token. `#0f172a`, `#2563eb`, and `#dc2626` are `slate-900`, `primary`, and `destructive`.

Conditional classes go through `cn` from `classnames`:

```tsx
className={cn(
  'h-12 flex-row items-center rounded-xl border bg-card px-3',
  error ? 'border-destructive' : 'border-input',
)}
```

Ui-kit variants are string maps keyed by a union (`ButtonVariant`), merged with `cn`. Cards and panels use `rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card`. The receipt screen splits the list at `max-w-[60%]` and the sidebar at `max-w-[40%]`.

`src/ui-kit/index.ts` (`lightTheme`) mirrors the Tailwind theme for props that cannot take a class, such as icon `color` and `placeholderTextColor`. Change a color in both files.

This is a landscape cashier. New tab screens fill the slot the tab layout already padded. Do not wrap them in another safe area, and do not rebuild the rail or header.

## Data

Screens and components do not call axios, `fetch`, or the generated API classes.

```tsx
const { getOrdersQuery, mutateDeleteReceipt } = useOrdersApi();
const { data: receipts = [] } = useQuery(getOrdersQuery());

mutateDeleteReceipt.mutate({
  params: { id },
  onSettledCallback: () => setIsDeleteModalOpen(false),
});
```

`getXQuery` is a TanStack `queryOptions` factory. Pass it to `useQuery`. Mutations are named `mutateX` and take `{ params, onSettledCallback }`. The SDK invalidates its own query key.

When the hook does not exist yet, add it in `api-sdk` under the Horpynka API SDK rule. Do not hand-roll the call in cashier.

- Session comes from `useSession()` in `@/src/contexts/auth-context`. Tokens go through `secureStoreService`.
- Forms use `react-hook-form`, `yupResolver`, and `yupService`. A field is `TextField` with `{...register('email')}`.
- Money is integer cents. Format it with `moneyService.toMoney`.
- Dates go through `dateFns` and `DATE_FORMATS` (Ukrainian locale). Components do not import `date-fns`.

Add shared client state as a Zustand slice, then spread it into `useStore`:

```ts
export const createReceiptStore: StateCreator<ReceiptsStore> = (set) => ({
  receipt: null,
  setReceipt: (receipt) => set(() => ({ receipt })),
});
```

Select one field: `useStore((s) => s.receipt)`.
